## post order

Write a function, _postOrder_, that takes in the root of a binary tree. The function should return
an array containing the post-ordered values of the tree.

[Post-order](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_traversal#Post-order,_LRN) traversal is when nodes are
recursively visited in the order: left child, right child, self.

#### test_00:

```js
const x = new Node('x');
const y = new Node('y');
const z = new Node('z');

x.left = y;
x.right = z;

//       x
//    /    \
//   y      z

postOrder(x);
// ['y', 'z', 'x']
```

